WEBVTT

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.640
Will you forgive me?

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.690
Wouldn't it be nice to play again?

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:14.710
Even if the strings break, the bond between you and this violin will never break.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:16.320
Bond?

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.260
String is "corda" in Italian.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:24.120
And corda also means "bond."

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.360
Corda... Bond...

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.100
Once More, Andante.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.370
Tsukimori-kun!

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:12.060
Hino?

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:14.000
Um...

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:15.770
What is it?

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:20.030
Please teach me how to string a violin!

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.890
You intend to start practicing again?

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:26.420
Yes! I've decided to try my best once again.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:26.950
So...

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.840
Tomorrow, wait in front of the train station at 10 AM.

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.550
I'm going to practice now. Later.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:37.700
Uh, wait...

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.720
At the train station?

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:51.760
What are you doing out there?

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.360
What song were you playing?

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:59.740
The high notes felt so transparent, like they were resonating inside my heart...

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:05.510
I didn't know the violin could sound this beautiful.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.500
She had the same eyes as back then.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:23.390
I wonder where he is taking me?

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:05.020
Good day.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.290
I apologize for not contacting you for a long time, Nakata-san.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:10.520
U-Um... Hello!

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:14.190
Oh, if it isn't the young master of the Tsukimori household.

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.600
It's been more than a year, hasn't it?

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:16.820
Yes.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:21.680
This is Nakata-san, a violin craftsman who has taken care of us since my grandmother's time.

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:25.250
He creates violins as well as repairing them.

00:04:25.250 --> 00:04:27.390
A violin craftsman...

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:31.920
I was hoping you could let us observe for a bit today, if it isn't too much trouble.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:37.870
Um, I'm a second year student at Seiso Academy just like Tsukimori-kun. My name is Kahoko Hino.

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:39.460
Pleased to meet you!

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.630
Well, I don't mind.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:45.100
Young lady, you play the violin as well, correct?

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:46.590
Yes.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:51.720
Watching me repair a violin isn't that interesting compared to playing one.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.270
That's...

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:59.490
This is quite broken, yes.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.320
But I can fix it, I can.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.400
This crack can be made whole again.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.490
Even if it breaks, that's not the end for it, I see.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:12.910
Yes. Unlike people, instruments can live on for many many years.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.400
As long as you take care of them, at least.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:18.650
How old is this one?

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:20.710
300 years old, about.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:21.960
300 years!

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:28.280
This one has passed through the hands of many a craftsman and has made music for a long time.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:32.560
If I don't fix it properly here, I will be dishonoring the ancestors that came before me.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:36.220
How long will it take to repair?

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:39.280
A number of months, or perhaps a year.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.700
That long?

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:46.740
Violins are made by hand, so no two are exactly the same. Repairs take a long time.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:51.330
Your violin is the only one of its kind in the world.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:59.330
In this world... One of a kind...

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.710
I shall grant you this!

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:12.010
That's right. This is the violin that contains Lili's feelings towards music, the only one in the world.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:20.140
I believe you should try letting Nakata-san look at your violin.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:25.040
During your performance 3 strings broke all at once.

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:27.210
I have no idea how much damage was done.

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:28.730
OK.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:44.590
I can't believe this.

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:52.220
Even though 3 strings broke at once, the body isn't warped and the pegs and sound board are flawless.

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:55.430
You're quite the spirited young lady, aren't you?

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.360
No, I'm not really...

00:06:57.360 --> 00:07:00.520
Not you, he's talking about the violin.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:01.650
Oh, is he?

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:05.110
That's odd...

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:07.820
There's no label.

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.240
Label?

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:11.680
It's stuck on the inside of the violin.

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:15.160
It's a mark that tells you who made the violin and where and when.

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.880
Will you look at that violin over there?

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:18.830
Sure.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:25.420
It's true.

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:30.380
I got my violin from Lili, so there's no label.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:34.460
But this violin has a pretty good face to it.

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:36.600
Please take good care of it, young lady.

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:37.910
I will!

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:43.230
Oh yes, young master. I just finished repairing that violin, however...

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:46.690
If you'd like, could you try it out for me?

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.030
Yes, I understand.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.160
Tsukimori-kun's Ave Maria.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:12.350
That's right. The first time I realized how beautiful the violin could be was from Tsukimori-kun's Ave Maria.

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.510
It's such a pretty sound.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:31.830
The sound has softened, hasn't it?

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:33.980
Because the repairs were a success?

00:08:33.980 --> 00:08:37.110
No, I'm talking about the young master's performance.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:44.670
Perhaps his performance is different because of who he is playing for?

00:09:03.450 --> 00:09:07.050
Thank you for bringing me with you, Tsukimori-kun.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:13.150
No, I just wanted you to learn more about the violin.

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:14.750
Sure.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:29.210
I have no need for people who can't decide and do everything halfway.

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:41.600
Oh my, welcome.

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.520
Hino!

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.570
And Tsukimori!

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:48.560
Tsuchiura-kun!

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:52.230
Hino, are you...

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:54.690
I came to buy some violin strings.

00:09:56.060 --> 00:09:59.030
I see, so you've decided to restring it.

00:09:59.260 --> 00:10:03.470
Yeah. I'm sorry about all that before, I'm OK now.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.580
Um, Tsukimori-kun...

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:12.410
I think the same kind of string as that violin from before would be nice.

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:15.660
The sound was really wonderful.

00:10:15.660 --> 00:10:17.970
I see. Then, over here.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:24.600
With this golden string still left, I need to replace the other three.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:27.730
I understand. First comes the G string.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.130
Tighten it a little more.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:37.180
I-I'm sorry!

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:38.190
No, it's...

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:41.120
Why am I blushing?

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:43.580
OK, next is the A string.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:57.340
It's been a long time since I've seen her smile like that.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:10:59.680
So she's made a comeback, then?

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:06.520
I've got to graduate from doing things halfway myself!

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:07.880
Finished.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:09.490
Next we need to tune it.

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:10.200
Right.

00:11:11.430 --> 00:11:15.050
Start from the A string. It's this "la" note.

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:17.230
OK.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.310
You didn't just hear that, OK?

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:36.460
Hino, relax your arm.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:37.290
OK.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:39.090
All right then, one more time.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:39.670
Right.

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:48.180
What a terrible sound, it's almost like I just started playing.

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:50.880
But that's only natural, I guess.

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:58.480
I love the violin. So I should just start over from the beginning.

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:02.410
Yes, from the beginning.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:30.100
Oh, you restrung the violin!

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:33.110
Yes, I did it myself.

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:35.060
Tsukimori-kun taught me how.

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.320
I see! Thank goodness!

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:38.440
Lili...

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.750
I'm so glad!

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:45.870
That's got to be the reason why you are able to see me.

00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:50.590
I'm sure all the practice you did up until now will be helpful to you.

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.470
I believe in that.

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:55.580
I'm going to do my best with this violin.

00:12:56.100 --> 00:13:01.930
After all, you gave me this violin, Lili, that's the only one in the entire world.

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:03.760
Kahoko Hino...

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.930
I'm going to do my best, and finish the competition.

00:13:08.760 --> 00:13:11.810
Aw, please don't cry like that.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:14.340
You're going to make me cry, too.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:18.970
I'm so glad I met this violin. Thank you, Lili.

00:13:18.970 --> 00:13:23.430
No, I'm the one who is grateful. Good luck, Kahoko Hino!

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:39.050
Calm down. Relax.

00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:42.680
Believe in all the practice you've done up until now.

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:51.340
That playing... Who is it?

00:13:51.340 --> 00:13:52.540
Could it be?

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:05.320
Kaho-chan!

00:14:06.730 --> 00:14:08.170
Hihara-sempai.

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:11.160
Thank goodness! You decided to continue playing the violin, I see!

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:15.160
Yes. I'm sorry I caused you to worry.

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:18.710
No, don't worry about it. I wasn't able to help.

00:14:18.980 --> 00:14:20.360
Hihara-sempai?

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:24.320
Um, anyway, did you hurt your fingers or something?

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:25.700
No...

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:27.010
But, that playing from before...

00:14:27.260 --> 00:14:29.240
It was awful, wasn't it?

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:31.550
But that's just the way I am now.

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:35.490
I love playing the violin.

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:40.020
I want to face the violin head on, while holding that feeling dear.

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:53.370
What a horrible performance. Almost like a beginner.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:54.660
Is it Hino?

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.200
Never a boring day with you, is there.

00:15:01.300 --> 00:15:08.040
So, Shimizu-kun... Have you decided on whether to do that interview or not? Are you listening?

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:12.510
Man, what a racket! Who the heck is playing that?

00:15:12.920 --> 00:15:14.760
Kaho-sempai.

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.310
Kaho-sempai?

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:20.020
Is that really Hino-san playing?

00:15:20.840 --> 00:15:21.810
Yes.

00:15:22.260 --> 00:15:24.950
That's Kaho-sempai's sound.

00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:27.860
It's different than her sound up until now.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.220
Fuyuumi-chan.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:32.410
Thank goodness, Kaho-sempai!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.300
Kaho-chan, you can do it!

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.400
OK, today's a celebration!

00:15:52.400 --> 00:15:55.300
Let's go to that new cake shop in front of the train station!

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:56.490
Roger that!

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.810
Don't forget to eat Kaho's portion, too!

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:01.890
Yeah!

00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:04.680
Is that Hino-san playing?

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:06.610
I heard a rumor that she changed violins, but...

00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:08.640
Did she change her technique?

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:10.950
In any case, isn't this a lot worse than she was?

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:12.260
She's terrible.

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:14.290
Indeed.

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:21.490
It seems like for someone from General Studies, if they don't play for just a little while they forget completely.

00:16:21.490 --> 00:16:23.370
She should have just withdrawn.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:28.610
And without Yunoki-sama participating, the competition is just going more and more downhill.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.970
Well, I'm happy to hear you say that, however...

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:32.610
Yunoki-sama!

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:39.690
It may not be a good performance, but when I see her trying her best I just have to protect her.

00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:40.930
If you'll excuse me...

00:17:01.780 --> 00:17:04.870
Relax more, Hino.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:23.520
Tsuchiura!

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:24.720
Yo.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.050
Thank you for everything.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:40.540
Tsuchiura...

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:42.440
You're quitting? Why?!

00:17:42.440 --> 00:17:44.090
Sasaki, that's enough.

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:45.140
But Captain...

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:54.130
I wanted to find out your conviction, Tsuchiura.

00:17:54.530 --> 00:17:58.070
Whether it's sports or music, the world of competition is harsh.

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:01.930
You'll never be able to overcome either if you can't focus on one.

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:03.770
Captain...

00:18:04.450 --> 00:18:07.560
If you're gonna do it, than you'd better win. Right, Tsuchiura?

00:18:08.440 --> 00:18:09.970
Thank you very much.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:15.600
Hino.

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:16.450
Tsuchiura-kun...

00:18:16.750 --> 00:18:18.280
Do you have a moment?

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:24.080
You're really trying hard.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:25.910
But I'm still terrible.

00:18:26.240 --> 00:18:28.930
I know what everyone has been saying.

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:33.950
But I decided to just work through it, step by step, without rushing.

00:18:36.390 --> 00:18:40.090
I'm really relieved that you came back.

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:52.270
I also have a bad memory of a competition.

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:59.310
It seems he still holds those irrational feelings from that competition long ago...

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:04.100
When I was in elementary school, I entered a competition just once.

00:19:05.130 --> 00:19:09.620
It wasn't just elementary students, but middle school and high school kids as well.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:12.150
It was a competition for anyone under 18.

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:14.130
A junior competition.

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:18.820
But the majority of the participants were high school students.

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:21.680
And I was the only elementary school kid.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:30.790
I played the best I could, and honestly speaking it was a better performance than anyone else gave.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:34.910
I just knew I had won.

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:41.520
But the person who won was one of the high school kids.

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:46.710
I got some special award that I didn't even know existed.

00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:48.730
Why?

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:50.110
Who knows?

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:54.850
It's probably because they didn't want to give the grand prize to some elementary school kid.

00:19:54.850 --> 00:19:59.570
I realize that music isn't really about competition.

00:19:59.570 --> 00:20:06.310
But back then it was as if my music, my everything, had been rejected.

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:08.460
Tsuchiura-kun...

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:13.440
Ever since then I quit playing the piano in front of others.

00:20:13.940 --> 00:20:19.030
That is, until that time I played the accompaniment to "Tristesse" during the first selection.

00:20:25.530 --> 00:20:31.870
Honestly, that was the first time I'd ever accompanied another instrument.

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:35.080
But when I played with you...

00:20:36.410 --> 00:20:40.800
I could feel the music inside of me grow.

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:50.320
My solitary piano playing... The door so tightly locked began to open.

00:20:54.980 --> 00:21:00.610
I can finally turn back to face the things I've been avoiding until now.

00:21:04.390 --> 00:21:08.370
Hino, it's all thanks to you, I'm grateful.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:10.370
Ts-Tsuchiura-kun...

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:21.510
It's painful to listen to!

00:21:22.580 --> 00:21:28.930
Don't you realize that your boorish playing is wasting the last precious moments we have with Yunoki-sama?

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:33.460
Is something the matter?

00:21:34.440 --> 00:21:36.030
Yunoki-sama!

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:41.570
Hino-san, you're really working hard, aren't you?

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:42.780
Um...

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:47.630
W-Well then, Yunoki-sama, if you'll excuse us.

00:21:47.630 --> 00:21:48.500
Oh?

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:57.140
Your playing has changed considerably.

00:21:57.860 --> 00:21:59.130
Um...

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:02.190
But there's another who has changed as well.

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:39.770
Lili's One Point Classic!

00:23:39.770 --> 00:23:44.310
In the world of music there are many words for different tempos.

00:23:44.310 --> 00:23:46.280
Andante is walking speed.

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:48.000
Allegro is rapid.

00:23:48.000 --> 00:23:50.980
And presto means extremely fast.

00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:56.190
There are lots of other tempo words like adagio and largo as well.

00:23:56.190 --> 00:23:57.860
OK, now time for a quiz.

00:23:57.860 --> 00:24:01.180
Since we're talking about tempos, take the metronome.

00:24:01.180 --> 00:24:05.090
Who was the first composer to utilize it?

00:24:05.810 --> 00:24:08.670
Hihara-sempai, you seem down today.

00:24:08.670 --> 00:24:10.860
Actually, you know the pork cutlet sandwich from the school store...

00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:12.260
He ate five of them today.

00:24:12.550 --> 00:24:15.040
He ate so much he's sleepy, I guess.

00:24:15.040 --> 00:24:17.270
Next episode: A Fanfare for You.

00:24:17.620 --> 00:24:20.100
A full course French dinner!

00:24:20.580 --> 00:24:24.110
The answer is... Beethoven!
